 "verdict": "screened - a Pareto move of the lead, not a reach move. The roller is deleted and the flank re-fit at the honest friction (mu 0.087, PA_kin 38): frozen exact Bench(110,360) 18.49 (score 93.28) vs the lead roller's 18.67 through the same Frozen class. Same reach (261/360, overhead 8/28) and the same 2 contact poses; +0.0018 in-band from the re-cut arm. Complexity 22.25 vs 24.25, one bought bearing fewer, 0 passive translations. With the lead's drive left unchanged the nose costs +0.10 at mu 0.05 and +1.23 at mu 0.087; the re-fit flank holds its fast number to mu 0.12. The +0.18 is below the 1-point rule: claim it as a simplification at equal score, not as a new lead by points. Kneeless + wedge control reproduced (21.18 flat / 20.12 wedged at mu 0.05; 21.76 / 20.70 at 0.087). The planar wedge cannot drop on the pin-knee lead (hub 3 already passes 0.38 mm over the skin at a fit pose).",
 "limiter": "Measured on the frozen claim: the lead's own walls. Fold 88 (overhead 14): K's dyad window a1max binds before the drive; the re-fit flank reaches dK 49.8, and even 52.8-60 at lower mu buys 0 poses. Knee slide 9 (overhead 4). Contact 2: the horn lug on hub K / the crank, at the lead's poses. Gap = reach 17.50 + in-band 0.45 + contact 0.54. Parts in band: hub3 0.739, L2 0.736, crank 0.818. Near-touch: 0.07 mm at the lead's pose (plane -60, elev 60, axial 105).",
 "note": "Search: the 160-config farm sweep (coarse1: nose radius x friction, wedge tau x psi, a random drive re-fit at mu 0.087), then CMA-ES on the farm. A = drive + nose at mu 0.087, 993 evals; B = + 11 seats, 1617; C = drive + nose at mu 0.05, 993. Convergence gate (2 mm objective, score points): A 0.00 / 0.00 / 0.00, B 0.36 / 0.31 / 0.12, C 0.00 / 0.00 / 0.00 - all pass. Friction enters as PA_kin = 43 - atan(mu) on both sides. A smaller nose lowers the horn PA at a given dK (~+2.3 deg of stroke per -0.5 mm of radius). Claim columns, frozen exact: lead drive mu 0 / 0.05 / 0.087 = 18.75 / 18.77 / 19.90; held out (mu 0.05) 23.73 = the lead's; A at mu 0.087 = 18.49. The mechanism record counts the ISO 8734 dowel as a bought part (22.25; the spec's 22.0 left it out). Loads, MVP1 (unpowered): clock spring 0.08 N.m + 0.03 N.m/rad gives ~9 N normal at r 15 mm. Hertz on O2.4 vs a convex 3.5 mm flank: ~340 MPa. Friction drag ~0.01-0.02 N.m vs R17's 1 N.m. Wear (Archard, k 1e-7, 1e6 cycles): ~1 um on the flank, ~14 um on the nose generatrix. Wear test at 5-15 N before CAD. The nose on DLC-coated Ti carries ~175 N static vs the MR63ZZ's ~70 N.",
